= Dither designs from September 2026 (fba_dither_auto) =

== Overview ==

`fba_dither_auto` (release 0.0.5) is now the script to run for dither designs.
It is self-contained, takes no `--dtver` and no `--stdsource`, and probes the
tile centre to decide which catalogs to use.  `fba_main_dither` and
`fba_cmx_new` remain for science tiles and for reference.

It replaces a choice that could not be made by hand: the main-survey star
catalog `GAIA_STD_FAINT` stops dead at Dec = -30, and the CMX catalogs are
frozen at 2020 and yield almost no flux standards.  Neither works everywhere.

Background: the April 2026 release selected dither stars with `STD_FAINT`, the
survey's ''spectrophotometric calibration'' bit -- about 60 per square degree,
so only a few hundred fibres landed on stars and the rest went to sky.  This
went unnoticed because every 0.0.3 test case was ''outside'' the DR9 footprint,
where the script already fell back to the dense Gaia catalog.  0.0.4 fixed it
with `--stdsource`; 0.0.5 removes the choice.

== The rule ==

{{{
main   GAIA_STD_FAINT, gaiadr2/1.0.0 backup        if >= --min-targets
cmx    STD_DITHER (dr9/0.49.0 cmx no-obscon), or
       STD_DITHER_GAIA (gaiadr2/0.49.0 cmx supp)   otherwise
}}}

The threshold asks about the '''main path only''': can the main catalog fill
this focal plane?  If yes, prefer it -- current catalogs, and every assigned
star is a flux standard.  If no, fall to CMX: ~10x denser, but frozen at 2020
and assigning almost no standards (127 against 833 at RA=46 Dec=+2).

`--min-targets` defaults to '''9000''', roughly where a design saturates the
4354 assignable fibres.  It is a preference, not a maximum: CMX is denser at
336 +30 (61103 against 9146) and is still not chosen.

'''Nothing is gated on the DESI footprint.'''  Both the main/CMX choice and the
CMX `no-obscon`/`supp` choice come from probing the catalogs.
`is_point_in_desi()` answers a different question -- at RA=305 Dec=-20 the tile
is inside the footprint, yet `no-obscon` holds 0 `STD_DITHER` and `supp` holds
70745 `STD_DITHER_GAIA`.  Under the old logic that tile failed outright.

=== Decisions at the September 2026 centres ===

|| '''centre''' || '''main''' || '''cmx''' || '''cmx supp''' || '''chosen''' ||
|| 336 +30 || 9146 || 61103 || 54657 || main ||
||   0 +30 || 3111 || 31850 || -- || cmx ||
||  15 +30 || 2514 || 24619 || -- || cmx ||
||  46  +2 || 1268 || 13422 || 12566 || cmx ||
||  46  -2 || 1206 || 12858 || 11671 || cmx ||
|| 305 -20 || 17238 || '''0''' || 70745 || main ||
||  80 -40 || '''0''' || 30554 || 25823 || cmx ||

At the same centre, seed and rundate it reproduces both original scripts
exactly: CMX at 46 +2 gives 3869 science / 127 standards / 450 sky, and main at
336 +30 gives 3439 / 3439 / 394, identical to `fba_cmx_new` and
`fba_main_dither` respectively.

== Where each path works ==

Sky map of both catalogs: `skymap/dither_coverage.png` in the repository.

'''`GAIA_STD_FAINT` stops dead at Dec = -30''' -- the DESI footprint's southern
limit.  Zero, not thinning.

|| '''Dec band''' || '''CMX usable''' || '''main usable''' ||
|| -90 to -40 || 100% || '''0%''' ||
|| -40 to -30 || 97% || 11% ||
|| -35 to -25 || 97% || 52% ||
|| -30 to -20 || 98% || 95% ||
||   0 to +20 || 100% || 99% ||

At >= 1000 targets per tile: 73% of sky either path works, '''27% CMX-only'''
(almost all the southern cap, plus the Galactic plane and the Magellanic
Clouds), 0% main-only.  Below Dec = -30 CMX is not a preference, it is the only
option.

'''Known limitation.'''  CMX designs read `dr9/0.49.0` skies, far sparser than
`1.0.0`: 6-18 sky fibres per petal at 80 -40 and 0 at 305 -20, against the 40
requested.  This is accepted; `verify_design.py` reports it as a NOTE and still
passes the design.

== Environment: pin desimodules/26.3 ==

'''`desimodules/main` cannot run these scripts as of September 2026.'''  Its
numpy 2.5.3 breaks `desitarget.io.write_mtl` on every MTL write: it does
`int(np.unique(release // 1000))`, which raises `TypeError` from numpy 2.4 on,
and `write_mtl` re-raises it as the misleading
`"Multiple data releases in MTL ([9])"` -- where `[9]` is a ''single'' release.
Reproducer: `dither_20260921/repro_write_mtl_numpy2.py`.

The scripts probe for this at startup and exit with an actionable message.

== Running ==

{{{
source /global/common/software/desi/desi_environment.sh 26.3

./fba_dither_auto --tilera 46 --tiledec -2 --tileid 84182 \
  --faflavor dithprec --rundate 2026-09-23T10:00:00+00:00 \
  --seed 80 --outdir ./084/
}}}

`--dry-run` reports the decision in about five seconds, light enough for a login
node.  `--force main|cmx` skips the probe.  Flavors: `dithprec`, `dithlost`,
`dithfocus`.

A full design (1 reference tile + 12 dithers) takes 3-5 minutes and writes about
300 MB, so run it in an allocation:

{{{
salloc --no-shell -A desi -C cpu -q interactive -t 04:00:00 -N 1 -J dither
JID=$(squeue -u $USER -h -n dither -o "%i")
srun --jobid=$JID -n1 -c 32 ./fba_dither_auto ...
}}}

Then check the written products, not the log:

{{{
python dither_20260921/verify_design.py <outdir> <reference tileid>
}}}

It handles either path, reports assigned fibres, stars, sky, `EXTRA` HDU
placement, the per-petal sky budget and the realised dither scatter, and exits
non-zero if anything is wrong.

== Repository ==

https://github.com/forero/dither_DESI/releases/tag/0.0.5

== Checking tiles into SVN ==

'''Check out into its own directory, never into one that already holds other
work.'''  `svn co <url> .` in a shared area such as `$SCRATCH` turns that whole
area into a working copy, after which `svn status` reports every unrelated
project directory as unversioned.

{{{
mkdir -p ~/tiles && cd ~/tiles
svn co https://desi.lbl.gov/svn/data/tiles/trunk/084
cd 084

cp /path/to/designs/fiberassign-0841??.fits.gz .
cp /path/to/designs/fiberassign-0841??.png .
svn add fiberassign-0841??.fits.gz fiberassign-0841??.png
svn status            # read this before committing
svn commit -m "Add dithprec fiberassign designs for tileids 084104-084181"
}}}

Do '''not''' use `svn status | grep '^?' | xargs svn add`: it adds everything
unversioned under the working copy root.

Last tileid committed: '''084103'''.  The September 2026 designs took
084104-084181, so the next free block starts at '''084182'''.

Browse: https://desi.lbl.gov/svn/data/tiles/trunk/084/
